      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find a general expression for \\( f(x) \\) that satisfies the given functional equation. The equation is:\n\n\\[\nf(x) + f\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{x}\\right) = \\log| x |.\n\\]\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = 2007 \\) into the equation:\n\n\\[\nf(2007) + f\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{2007}\\right) = \\log| 2007 |.\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\nf(2007) + f\\left(\\frac{2006}{2007}\\right) = \\log 2007.\n\\]\n\nNext, let's denote \\( y = \\frac{2006}{2007} \\) so we have:\n\n\\[\nf(2007) + f(y) = \\log 2007.\n\\]\n\nSuppose \\( f(y) = \\log | y | \\). This is because \\( y \\) is the reciprocal of \\( x \\) minus 1, and the functional equation suggests that \\( f(x) \\) is likely related to \\( \\log | x | \\).\n\nTo verify, if \\( f(y) = \\log | y | \\), then:\n\n\\[\nf(2007) + \\log | \\frac{2006}{2007} | = \\log 2007.\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\( | \\frac{2006}{2007} | = \\frac{2006}{2007} \\), thus:\n\n\\[\n\\log | 2007 | - \\log | 2007 | = 0}.\n\\]\n\nSince we are asked for a non-zero solution, we consider the negative scenario where \\( f(y) = -\\log | y | \\). This also satisfies the given functional equation:\n\n\\[\nf(2007) + (-\\log | 2006 |) = \\log | 2007 |\n\\]\n\nThus, the function \\( R: f(2007) = \\log | 2007 | \\) provided by simplification thus correctly.\n\nThus, the value of \\( 2007 \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\log 2007}\n\\]",
